DECISION_RECORD_GPU_SELF_WITNESS_001
STATUS     := PROPOSED for DECIDE (Claude records Devon's statement; Devon decides; Codex applies)
DATE       := 2026-10-21 17:09 America/New_York
STATEMENT  := Devon: "The point of this project is to run on the GPU as close to metal as possible.
              Adding another board to provide outside attestation is unnecessary.
              The GPU witnesses itself as the game world."
GOVERNS    := O_GENESIS_CAPTURE and O_COMMIT of SPEC-FLAG-WORLD-FIRST-TICK-001 (FT v0.1.1 73429D78…),
              under SPEC-WITNESS-FACE-G-READOUT-001 v0.1.0 (057C30E2…) and DECISION_RECORD_FLAG_WORLD_D_G_001 (3419D528…).
SOURCES    := GRL :113-119 (configuration := (arrangement, admissibility witness); the pair is the world object);
              FT :52 (readback exposes the constituted successor), :164-167 (output projection: receipt + state with chain),
              :196-197 (tick record, ONE new link); Paper B commit law (RETURN (program, state_{t+1}));
              TRACE_CONTINUITY_SHAPE §4 ("it witnesses itself": the 720-overlap record IS the admission witness).
              JTP :22 governs the Tang/VF2 hardware worldline. It is NOT the game world's worldline.

BINDS
  GAME_WORLD_WORLDLINE := the GPU-resident chain of committed (field, witness) pairs on carrier 012 (FT :164-167, :196-197).
  WITNESS              := the GPU's own 720-overlap record for the committed field, walls included. No external attester.
  COMMIT               := the GPU appends ONE chain link := (field, witness, receipt) with predecessor custody by hash
                          (FT :196-197; RECEIPT_READING_001). This IS COMMITTED for the game world.
  EVENT_RECORD         := the captured JTP frame 4472CFC5…7228B: its header names Junction("17") between Domain("4")
                          and Domain("9"). The frame is the event's record; its locus is the header's vertex (NOTE_O_GENESIS_CAPTURE_LOCUS).
  GENESIS_FIELD (g₁)   := on 012: the 12 site-support flags of Junction("17") read THIS; all other flags read NO
                          (FT :51; Codex 17:03, derived without payload indexing or identifier ordering).
  PREDECESSOR (x_t)    := Ground₀(012), B263644E59A696999C02DFD25386A5ABEFDB2D0FC4317A0FE2CCCD90502EBAD3.

NOT_SAME
  The Tang/VF2 JTPClosureV1 append (JTP :22) is the HARDWARE lane's commit. It is NOT a gate on the game world.
  The game world does not report the LED receipt as committed either; it commits its OWN pair on the GPU.
  Outside attestation is unnecessary BECAUSE the configuration carries its witness (GRL dependent pair).

APPLY (Codex, on DECIDE)
  1. current := g₁ as bound above. Commit the genesis pair on the GPU as ONE chain link over Ground₀ (predecessor hash B263644E…).
  2. Then the handoff RUN-THROUGH, unchanged: O_D_G_FROM_BYTES → O_FACE_READ_20 → O_J17_ROLE (check {G,S}) →
     triad_position (FAB :44) → STEP_FABRIC → RETURN (program, state_{t+1}) → commit → CONFORM V1/V2.
  3. Stop ONLY at: NOT_SAME against promoted bytes; a MAYBE tie on a face J17 is in; O_S_F_BINDING; repository commit/push/seal.

OPEN (report, do not block)
  O_S_F_BINDING (Devon). O_FLEX_MOTIF_CORRESPONDENCE. The hardware lane's own JTP append remains that lane's O_next.
